<p>In February 1879, the Northern Pacific Railroad laid track directly on the frozen Missouri River. Railcars carried construction materials to the relatively level lowlands on the west bank, where a new townsite was being platted under the direction of Northern Pacific division engineer {% person "thomas-rosser" %}Thomas Rosser{% endperson %}. After completing the plat, Rosser used his business car as a real-estate office and sold lots to the public.</p>

<p>Mandan served as headquarters of the Missouri Division, which extended 200 miles from the Missouri River to the Yellowstone River at Glendive, Montana. A July 1879 contract with Smith &amp; French for section houses and water tanks also called for a depot in Mandan. It was built south of Main Street at Stark Avenue, later renamed Collins Avenue.</p>

